Upscaling experiment was conducted under the similar conditions in a home-made reactor. Briefly, a mixture of acetonitrile $(20~\mathrm{ml})$ ), water $20~\mathrm{ml}$ ) and benzene $(440\upmu\mathrm{L}$ , $5\mathrm{\mmol}$ ) was transferred into the home-made reactor containing $100~\mathrm{{mg}}$ of catalyst. The resulting biphasic system was stirred with dropwise addition of hydrogen peroxide $(30~\mathrm{wt\%}$ , $390\upmu\mathrm{L}$ , 3.8mmol) and irradiated with a 300 W Xe lamp with a UV-cut filter to remove light with wavelengths less than $420~\mathrm{nm}$ and an IR-cut filter to remove all wavelengths longer than $800\ \mathrm{nm}$ . After the reaction, the process of treatment and products detection are similar to the previous reported.
The labeling experiments were performed over benzene and benzene- $\cdot d_{6}$ , respectively, under standard reaction conditions. The kinetic isotope effect (KIE) is defined as $k_{\mathrm{H}}/k_{\mathrm{D}}.$ , in which $k_{\mathrm{H}}$ and $k_{\mathrm{{D}}}$ is the rate constant for the benzene hydroxylation reaction carried out over benzene and benzene- $.d_{6}$ respectively.
